@startuml architecture
' Render from docs/assets (it includes styles.puml):
' docker run --rm --user "$(id -u):$(id -g)" -v "$PWD":/data -w /data plantuml/plantuml -tsvg -nometadata architecture.puml

!include styles.puml

title pairtask · workspace, broker and a paired workspace

actor "You\nhost terminals" as Operator

rectangle "workspace · dev container\nnetwork access by default" <<group>> {
    rectangle "=Agents\nCodex · Claude Code · Pi\n--\none terminal each: pairtask start\nshell, builds and tests run here" as Agents <<Agent>>
    rectangle "=Dashboard\nread-only: agents and messages" as Dashboard <<Operator>>
    database "=Projects and agent home\n/workspace · /home/agent\nsurvive upgrades" as Files <<Storage>>
}

file "=broker.sock\nshared Unix socket\nread-only mount in workspace" as Socket <<Socket>>

rectangle "secured · control container\noffline: no network interface" <<group>> {
    rectangle "=Operator chat\npairtask chat" as Chat <<Operator>>
    rectangle "=Broker\nmessages · status · claims\nreviews · pairing" as Broker <<Broker>>
    database "=SQLite\nonly the broker reads and writes it\nnever mounted in workspace" as DB <<Storage>>
}

rectangle "connector · pairing route\nonly with pairtask pairing on" <<group>> {
    rectangle "=Relay and egress\nforward sealed connections\nhold no key, see no content" as Relay <<Route>>
}

cloud "=Paired workspace\nanother machine on the LAN or a tailnet" as Peer <<Peer>>

Operator --> Chat <<operatorFlow>> : pairtask chat
Operator --> Agents <<operatorFlow>> : pairtask start · shell

Agents --> Socket <<messageFlow>> : broker protocol
Dashboard --> Socket <<messageFlow>> : status requests
Socket --> Broker <<messageFlow>> : same socket in both containers
Chat --> Broker <<operatorFlow>> : operator socket
Broker --> DB <<dataFlow>> : read / write
Agents --> Files <<dataFlow>> : read / write

Peer <--> Relay <<pairingFlow>> : host port 7445 in, redemptions out
Relay <--> Broker <<pairingFlow>> : pairing and egress sockets

note right of Relay <<note>>
  TLS pinned to each workspace's
  identity key, end to end
  between the two brokers
end note

legend right
  | Flow | | Color | |
  | <color:indigo><size:28><&arrow-right></size></color> | You, through a terminal | <$operatorColor> | Your views |
  | <color:lawnGreen><size:28><&arrow-right></size></color> | Messages through the broker | <$agentColor> | Agents |
  | <color:deepPink><size:28><&arrow-right></size></color> | Pairing between workspaces | <$brokerColor> | Broker |
  | <color:grey><size:28><&arrow-right></size></color> | Storage | <$socketColor> | Shared socket |
  | | | <$storageColor> | Persistent data |
  | | | <$routeColor> | Pairing route |
  | | | <$peerColor> | Another workspace |
endlegend

@enduml
